{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ובארצכם לא תעשו", :translit "u-v'artzchem lo ta'asu", :gloss "and in your land you shall not do"} {:he "ומיד בן נכר לו", :translit "u-miyad ben nechar lo", :gloss "and from the hand of a foreigner"} {:he "לסרס", :translit "l'sares", :gloss "to castrate"} {:he "עכו\"ם", :translit "akum", :gloss "idolater"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Smikhut parshiyot: the verse about not doing castration in your land is immediately followed by 'and from the hand of a foreigner,' teaching the prohibition extends even when done through a non-Jew"}], :frame {:text "The Sifra on the verse 'and in your land you shall not do' (Leviticus 22:24) derives that the prohibition of castration applies throughout one's land and not only in the Temple context. The Talmud in Shabbat 85b discusses the broader scope of the prohibition of s'risah (castration). The halakhic principle that a Jew may not use a non-Jew as an agent for a forbidden act is addressed in Kiddushin 41a.", :sources ["Sifra Leviticus 22:24" "Shabbat 85b" "Kiddushin 41a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Smikhut parshiyot: the verse about not doing castration in your land is immediately followed by 'and from the hand of a foreigner,' teaching the prohibition extends even when done through a non-Jew", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:24:56.481831030Z", :model "glm-5.2"}